# ── Security headers (site-wide) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# frame-ancestors 'none' blocks clickjacking overlays on the OAuth login modal;
# X-Frame-Options is the legacy fallback for the same. HSTS pins https (the
# site is https-only behind Cloudflare). Full CSP is deferred post-GA — the
# static export leans on inline styles/scripts and needs a nonce strategy.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# Next's static export emits the OG share card as an extensionless file
# (/opengraph-image), which Cloudflare serves as application/octet-stream —
# so iMessage/Twitter/Slack refuse to render it and fall back to the tiny
# no-photo preview. Force the real image content-type so the card shows.
/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/*/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# ── Versioned data shards: immutable long-lived cache ────────────────────────
# The client fetches these WITH a ?v=<lastCrawl> query param (force-cache), so
# every URL is already cache-busted per crawl — a new crawl is a new URL. Yet
# Cloudflare Pages serves them with `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`, so
# each load pays a revalidation round-trip for nothing. Freeze them.
#
# _headers matches on PATH, not query string, so these globs match the whole
# family (lots-0.json … lots-5.json AND lots-index.json; sold-archive-0/1.json
# AND sold-archive-index.json; sold-ledger-0/1.json AND sold-ledger-index.json)
# — all of which are ?v=<lastCrawl>-busted in useRayData.ts (loadFull,
# loadSoldArchive, loadSoldLedger). sold-ledger-* was missing from this list
# until Sep 2 2026 and revalidated on every /profile load for nothing.
#
# Deliberately NOT `/data/ray/*.json` (too broad): the phase-1 files
# meta/upcoming/stats/market/backtest.json are fetched WITHOUT ?v= (L179-183)
# and MUST keep revalidating to pick up a new crawl. players.json / refs.json
# likewise stay untouched. These name-prefixed globs match none of them.
/data/ray/lots-*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/data/ray/sold-archive-*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/data/ray/sold-ledger-*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
